d}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a7f69c-4b83-50f9-933c-1fa3c60a2e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531803} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6bb199-c4f1-5942-aa25-3201086ffc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531807} {:answer/id #uuid "4bde3cba-d7a2-5b3d-bcfc-510fcdbe781e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531814} {:answer/id #uuid "ca8d0cf4-25d1-56ab-94d5-7f2008bec7af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531832} {:answer/id #uuid "d97e42ef-dfa1-5464-a6f5-bdc6b4e0564d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531833}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531833} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f73a17e-5f4d-5c48-88d9-7569eef6e206" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b4051a5d-c9b9-518f-92fa-031fa84284a7" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v,\\,u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 0,\\,1\\le v\\le 2}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\nF(r(u,v))=⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩=5 u + 6 v + 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(5 u + 6 v + 3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}[v \\left(5 u + 3 v + 3\\right)]_{v=1}^{v=2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}(5 u + 12)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =[\\frac{u \\left(5 u + 24\\right)}{2}]_{-3}^{0} \\\\ & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4b1fd0e-7c9a-5d70-bf10-5e02ccfe0ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{146}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533108}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533108} :answer-field/id #uuid "6728a9ae-96e5-56bc-8253-87e573add42c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3f226a42-1c19-5b1b-9c9d-b7e534c60692" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the triangle spanned by $a=⟨4,-5,-3⟩$ and $b=⟨-1,1,-5⟩.$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =((-5)\\cdot (-5)-(-3)\\cdot 1)i-(4\\cdot (-5)-(-3)\\cdot (-1))j+(4\\cdot 1-(-5)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =28i+23j-k \\\\  & =⟨28,23,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{28}^{2}+{23}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{784+529+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1314} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{146}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{146}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533101 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75bd512d-925b-5abd-a73f-5e9f381c0b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{301}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533103}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533103} :answer-field/id #uuid "4255caa3-50ba-54fa-82a8-74962672c0b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6cf72a6b-7f5c-53ee-89c4-60c564528c1e" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the triangle spanned by $p=⟨-3,6,0⟩$ and $q=⟨4,3,-6⟩.$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\times q & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(6\\cdot (-6)-0\\cdot 3)i-((-3)\\cdot (-6)-0\\cdot 4)j+((-3)\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =-36i-18j-33k \\\\  & =⟨-36,-18,-33⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,p\\times q\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-36)^{2}+(-18)^{2}+(-33)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1296+324+1089} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2709} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{301}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{301}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2940bc66-6dca-54fe-86c2-cce56dcbff76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{82}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533086} {:answer/id #uuid "41beb57f-56fd-5175-8fe2-8ca34d908f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "35\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533090} {:answer/id #uuid "475d93f6-73c1-5b0e-9699-aa6b252a3217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533092} {:answer/id #uuid "628b5ec7-d093-5db0-8e50-e8d9010441b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{929}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533097} {:answer/id #uuid "699110fa-ecec-5d60-ac7c-16ebeb43f741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1921}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533099}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533092} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed3fc811-9e82-50bd-a79a-fa353e5ebb51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b36fd647-10f7-545b-9943-caa2a786ad1f" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $r=⟨-5,4,5⟩$ and $t=⟨6,3,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\times t & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -5 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-5 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(4\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot 3)i-((-5)\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot 6)j+((-5)\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 6)k \\\\  & =-23i+20j-39k \\\\  & =⟨-23,20,-39⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,r\\times t\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-23)^{2}+{20}^{2}+(-39)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{529+400+1521} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2450} \\\\  & =35\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"}]}
